          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong limited principle of omniscience
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            ) states that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
            is again decidable. That is,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\forall x, P(x) \vee \neg{P(x)}) \Rightarrow (\exists x, P(x)) \vee \neg(\exists x, P(x)) ,
          %p or equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\forall x, P(x) \vee \neg{P(x)}) \Rightarrow (\exists x, P(x)) \vee (\forall x, \neg{P(x)}) .
          %p
            We have not stated the domain of quantification of the variable
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            corresponding to a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            and apply this principle to the constantly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            proposition, then the subsingleton is decidable follows, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, P(x)
            holds, then either the subsingleton is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists x, P(x)
            holds, or the subsingleton is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, \neg P(x)
            holds. Thus, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            holds for all subsingletons implies
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EM
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi EM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EM
            implies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            (over any domain). However, Bishop's
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            takes the domain to be the set of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
            based on infinite-time
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Turing+machine"} Turing machine
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            but not
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EM
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Bauer11"} Bauer (2011)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists x, P(x)
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is decidable are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+truth+values"} open truth values
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rosolini+dominance"} Rosolini dominance
          %p
            We can also state the principle set-theoretically, with explicit reference to the domain of quantification. Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong
              limited principle of omniscience for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi LPO
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO_A
            ) states that, given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+map"} constant map
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            belongs to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO_{\mathbb{N}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequence"} infinite sequence
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bits"} bits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            corresponding to a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            and this principle is applied to the constant function at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is decidable, since if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x. f(x) = 1
            holds, then either the subsingleton is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists x. f(x) = 1
            holds, or the subsingleton is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x.f(x) = 0
            holds.
          %p
            While
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            is a classic example of the difference between constructive and classical mathematics,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            holds for the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{N}}
            of
            = succeed "s;" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+natural+number"} extended natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{N}}
            may constructively be given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            topology. See
            %a{:href => "#Escardo11"} Escardó (2011)
            for this and much more.
          %h3#in_the_antithesis_interpretation In the antithesis interpretation
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antithesis+interpretation"} antithesis interpretation
            of constructive mathematics, propositions are functions from from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+of+truth+values"} set of truth values
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \mapsto f(x) = b
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mutually+exclusive+propositions"} mutually exclusive
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction+principle"} induction principle
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨆
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigsqcup_{x \in A} (b \mapsto f(x) = b)
            is mutually exclusive and affirmative and the the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨅
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigsqcap_{x \in A} (b \mapsto f(x) = b)
            is mutually exclusive and refutative. The
            %strong
              limited principle of omniscience for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi LPO
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO_A
            ) states that, given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨆
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigsqcup_{x \in A} (b \mapsto f(x) = b)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨅
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigsqcap_{x \in A} (b \mapsto f(x) = b)
            is decidable.
          %h3#using_exclusive_disjunction Using exclusive disjunction
          %p
            There is an equivalent version of the limited principle of omniscience which uses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exclusive+disjunction"} exclusive disjunction
            instead of the inclusive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            for the definition of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
          %p
            The
            %strong limited principle of omniscience
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LPO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO
            ) states that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
            on a sete
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is again decidable. That is,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\forall x \in A, P(x) \underline{\vee} \neg{P(x)}) \Rightarrow (\exists x \in A, P(x)) \underline{\vee} \neg(\exists x \in A, P(x)) ,
          %p or equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\forall x \in A, P(x) \underline{\vee} \neg{P(x)}) \Rightarrow (\exists x, P(x)) \underline{\vee} (\forall x, \neg{P(x)}) .
          %p
            We can also state the principle set-theoretically, with explicit reference to the domain of quantification. Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong
              limited principle of omniscience for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi LPO
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO_A
            ) states that, given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+map"} constant map
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            belongs to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall f \in \{0,1\}^A, (\exists x \in A, f(x) = 1) \underline{\vee} \neg(\exists x \in A, f(x) = 1) ,
          %p or equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ̲
