              holds.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By the equivalence of the definitions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
              using inclusive disjunction and exclusive disjunction, the versions of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_A
              using inclusive and exclusive disjunctions are equivalent to each other.
            %p
              In dependent type theory, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exclusive+disjunction"} exclusive disjunction
              of two types is formulated as the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %munder
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo ̲
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                        %mi B
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                        %mi B
                    %mi x
