          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+Tarski+universe"} univalent Tarski universe
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
              closed under dependent product types, dependent sum types, and identity types and satisfying the axiom of infinity and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              implies the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              One can construct an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}:U
              representing the
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(\mathbb{R})
              is a sequentially Cauchy complete Archimedean ordered field which satisfies the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+LPO"} analytic LPO
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              for the entire type theory. Thus, any univalent Tarski universe which has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              or a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+operator"} choice operator
              for the types in the universe also implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              for the entire type theory.
          %p
            Note that in all these cases, the real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            constructed from these universes or classical models of foundations of mathematics, while equivalent to the internal Dedekind real numbers constructed in the universe or model, are not necessarily equivalent to the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            in the foundations.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+sigma-frame"}
                initial
                = succeed "-frame" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-overt" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            for
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            says that for any set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and any entire
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:A \times B \to \Sigma
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            there exists a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, f(x)) = \top
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The proof is similar to one direction of the proof of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu-Goodman-Myhill+theorem"} Diaconescu-Goodman-Myhill theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be a
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟚
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 = 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/if+and+only+if"} if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              holds, resulting in a set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟚
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝟚
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to \mathbb{2}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, f(x)) = \top
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is precisely
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
            The full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            for
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and any entire
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:A \times B \to \Sigma
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            there exists a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, f(x)) = \top
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              implies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              for
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              stated above, which in turn implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+bar+theorem"} full bar theorem
              implies the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#Diener18"} Diener 2018
            for more statements that imply
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+type+theory"} triangulated type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
            imply the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Suppose that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-frame"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  \-frame
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              holds.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-frame"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  \-frame
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete"} discrete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflection"} coreflection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \mathbb{I}
              is also a
              = succeed "-frame," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \mathbb{I}
              is in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              in triangulated type theory, this implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              in the discrete mode of simplicial type theory. Triangulated type theory satisfies the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+cohesion"}
                  axiom of
                  = succeed "-coheson" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕀
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              = succeed "-null," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕀
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+punctual+cohesion"} axiom of punctual cohesion
              because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+type"} pointed type
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Shulman18"} Shulman 2018
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              in the discrete mode implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              in the non-discrete mode.
          %h3#statements_inconsistent_with_
            Statements inconsistent with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
            There are various statements in mathematics which are inconsistent with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonicity"} canonicity
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+canonicity"} homotopy canonicity
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝟚
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{2}
              to the booleans
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟚
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(n) = 1
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 n + 2
              is the sum of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(n) = 0
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 n + 2
              is not the sum of two prime numbers, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 n + 2
              being the sum of two prime numbers is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decidable proposition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goldbach%27s+conjecture"} Goldbach's conjecture
              states that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is equal to the constant sequence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mn .1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda n:\mathbb{N}.1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Goldbach
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}(\mathrm{Goldbach}, 0, 1):\mathbb{N}
              which is 0 or 1 according as the Goldbach conjecture is true or false. This term is not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identified with
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+form"} canonical form
              (a numeral), contradicting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+canonicity"} homotopy canonicity
              and by extension
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonicity"} canonicity
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brouwer%27s+continuity+principle"} Brouwer's continuity principle
              for any one of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book+real+numbers"} HoTT book real numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
              defined using the initial
              = succeed "-frame" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              implies that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_H
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
              are equivalent to each other, which means we can simply denote this set of real numbers as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-order"} pseudo-order
              relation on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              is decidable. As a result, we can define a pointwise-discontinuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}
              by case analysis
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = 1
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = 1
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}
              are pointwise-continuous.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              In the presence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+countable+choice"} weak countable choice
              axiom
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N}, 2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brouwer%27s+continuity+principle"} Brouwer's continuity principle
              for the usual impredicative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
              defined using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+truth+values"} frame of truth values
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N}, 2}
              implies that the Cauchy real numbers and the Dedekind real numbers coincide. Since the previous theorem implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brouwer%27s+continuity+principle"} Brouwer's continuity principle
              for the Cauchy real numbers,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N}, 2}
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brouwer%27s+continuity+principle"} Brouwer's continuity principle
              for the Dedekind real numbers.
          %p
            This means that theories which accept both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brouwer%27s+continuity+principle"} Brouwer's continuity principle
            for the Dedekind real numbers, such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (infinity,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+infinity-groupoids"} Euclidean-topological infinity-groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N}, 2}
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+sigma-frame"}
                initial
                = succeed "-frame" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is equivalent to the fact that the unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              to the initial
              = succeed "-frame" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+negation"} logical negation
              function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \neg x
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              does not satisfy the linear interpolation condition for Phoa’s principle for the booleans; it is not true that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¬
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∨
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg x = (\neg 0) \wedge (x \vee \neg 1) = 1 \wedge (x \vee 0) = x
              on the booleans. As a result,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with Phoa’s principle for the initial
              = succeed "-frame" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with synthetic quasi-coherence (i.e. the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kock-Lawvere+axiom"} Kock-Lawvere axiom
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+sigma-frame"}
                initial
                = succeed "-frame" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a finitely presented
              = succeed "-algebra," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
              equivalent to the quotient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mi …
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma[x_1 \ldots x_n]
              by finitely many relations, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}_\Sigma(A)
              be the set of
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto (f \mapsto f(a)):A \to \Sigma^{\mathrm{Spec}_\Sigma(A)}
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Synthetic quasi-coherence for the
              %span.newWikiWord
                initial
                = succeed "-frame" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/initial+objectsigma-frame"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              implies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              %br/
          %p
          .num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              is not the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+sigma-frame"}
                initial
                = succeed "-frame" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+type+theory"} triangulated type theory
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The directed interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+type+theory"} triangulated type theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              being a
              = succeed "-frame" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              as proven above.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              then implies that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+sigma-frame"}
                initial
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                \-frame
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
              because of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunction"} endofunction
              on the boolean domain.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
              is inconsistent with the existence of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Specker+sequence"} Specker sequence
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#Diener18"} Diener 2018
            for more statements that are inconsistent with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LPO
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LPO}_\mathbb{N}
          %h3#models Models
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Assuming that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi LPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LPO_{\mathbb{N}}
                (the LPO for natural numbers) holds in any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                and indeed in any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^N
                is a constant object.
            %li
              %p
                The LPO for natural numbers fails in Johnstone’s
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+topos"} topological topos
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+omniscience"} principle of omniscience
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limited+principle+of+omniscience"} weak limited principle of omniscience
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lesser+limited+principle+of+omniscience"} lesser limited principle of omniscience
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov%27s+principle"} Markov's principle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
          %h2#references  References
          %ul
            %li#Bishop67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Errett+Bishop"}> Errett Bishop
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Foundations+of+Constructive+Analysis"} Foundations of Constructive Analysis
              %blockquote
                %p (in the introduction or chapter 1, I forget)
            %li#Ishihara06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hajime+Ishihara"}> Hajime Ishihara
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reverse Mathematics in Bishop’s Constructive Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4000/philosophiascientiae.406"} doi:10.4000/philosophiascientiae.406
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://philosophiascientiae.revues.org/pdf/406"} pdf
            %li{:id => "LombardiQuitté2010"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Lombardi"}> Henri Lombardi
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Quitt%C3%A9"} Claude Quitté
                (2010):
                %em Commutative algebra: Constructive methods (Finite projective modules)
                Translated by Tania K. Roblo, Springer (2015) (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-017-9944-7"}> doi:10.1007/978-94-017-9944-7
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hlombardi.free.fr/CACM.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rathjen13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rathjen"}> Michael Rathjen
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Constructive Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory and the limited principle of omniscience
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.3037"} arXiv:1302.3037
            %li#Shulman18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem in real-cohesive homotopy type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.07584"} arXiv:1509.07584
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129517000147"} doi:10.1017/S0960129517000147
            %li#Diener18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hannes+Diener"}> Hannes Diener
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructive reverse mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.05495"} arXiv:1804.05495
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dspace.ub.uni-siegen.de/handle/ubsi/1306"} dspace:ubsi/1306
            %li#Booij20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Auke+Booij"}> Auke Booij
                ,
                %em Analysis in univalent type theory
                (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://etheses.bham.ac.uk/id/eprint/10411"}> etheses:10411
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/id/eprint/10411/7/Booij2020PhD.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ciraulo22
              %p
                Francesco Ciraulo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                    \-locales in Formal Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-18%281%3A7%292022"} doi:10.46298/lmcs-18%281%3A7%292022
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.09644"} arXiv:1801.09644
            %li#Rijke22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082"} arXiv:2212.11082
            %li#BirchfieldSwan24
              %p
                Madeleine Birchfield, Andrew Swan (2024) on Category Theory Zulip,
                %a{:href => "https://categorytheory.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/229199-learning.3A-questions/topic/LPO.20and.20sigma-frame.20structure.20on.20booleans"} LPO and sigma-frame structure on booleans
            %li#Grossack24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Grossack"}> Chris Grossack
                ,
                %em Life in Johnstone’s Topological Topos 3 – Bonus Axioms
                (
                %a{:href => "https://grossack.site/2024/07/03/topological-topos-3-bonus-axioms"}> web
                )
            %li#LombardiMahboubi24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Lombardi"}> Henri Lombardi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assia+Mahboubi"} Assia Mahboubi
                %em Théories géométriques pour l’algèbre des nombres réels sans test de signe ni axiome de choix dépendant
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.15218"}> arXiv:2406.15218
                )
          %p This reference calls the fully untruncated limited principle of omniscience for the natural numbers simply by the term “limited principle of omniscience”. However, the limited principle of omniscience usually refers to the fully truncated version.
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              Univalent Foundations Project,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013)
          %p
            These two references call the limited principle of omniscience simply by the term “principle of omniscience” or “omniscience principle”. However,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+omniscience"} principle of omniscience
            can refer to multiple possible axioms.
          %ul
            %li#Bauer11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"} Andrej Bauer
                (2011) via constructivenews,
                %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/06/injection.pdf"}
                  An Injection from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}^{\mathbb{N}}
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                (pdf)
            %li#Escardo11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"} Martín Escardó
                (2011) via constructivenews,
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/papers/omniscient-2011-07-06.pdf"} Infinite sets that satisfy the principle of omniscience in all varieties of constructive mathematics
                (pdf)
